In Angular, a shared component is a reusable component that can be used across multiple modules and applications. Here are the steps to create a shared component in Angular:

1. Create a new folder for your shared components:

In the root of your project, create a new folder named `shared` (or any other name you prefer). This folder will contain all your shared components.
2. Create a new component:

Inside the `shared` folder, create a new folder named `components` (or any other name you prefer). Inside this folder, create a new component using the Angular CLI:
```bash
ng generate component my-shared-component
```
This will create a new component named `my-shared-component` with a corresponding HTML and TypeScript file.

3. Define the component:

Open the `my-shared-component.component.ts` file and define the component using the `@Component` decorator:
```typescript
import { Component } from '@angular/core';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-my-shared-component',
  template: '<p>Shared component: {{ title }}</p>'
})
export class MySharedComponent {
  title = 'Shared Component';
}
```
In this example, we've defined a simple component with a template that displays the `title` property.

4. Use the component in a module:

To use the shared component in a module, you need to declare it in the `declarations` array of the module. For example, let's say you want to use the component in the `AppModule`:
```typescript
import { NgModule } from '@angular/core';
import { CommonModule } from '@angular/common';
import { MySharedComponent } from './shared/components/my-shared-component';

@NgModule({
  declarations: [MySharedComponent],
  imports: [CommonModule],
  exports: [MySharedComponent]
})
export class AppModule {}
```
In this example, we've declared the `MySharedComponent` in the `declarations` array and exported it using the `exports` array.

5. Use the component in a component:

To use the shared component in another component, you can simply use the component's selector in the HTML template:
```html
<!-- app.component.html -->
